Peer Review Dashboard – Randomized Encounter Selection Overview

This SQL script powers the Peer Review Dashboard by selecting randomized encounters per provider on a quarterly basis. It is designed to streamline peer review processes and support automation by pulling 8 distinct, 
randomly selected patient encounters per provider per quarter, excluding non-billable or incomplete visits.

Key Logic
Randomization: Each run of the script refreshes the patient list using NEWID() to generate a new randomized order of eligible visits.
Quarterly Grouping: Encounters are grouped by year and quarter for time-based segmentation.
Data Scope: The script only includes data from the previous 12 months, filtering by encounter timestamp.

Visit Criteria: 
Only completed and billable visits are included (billable_ind = 'Y').
Non-encounters are excluded using timestamp and billing indicators.
Only encounters with a valid provider (provider_id present) are included.

Enhancements & Features:
Random Sampling: Selects 8 visits per provider, per quarter across various service lines: Behavioral Health (BH), Mental Health (MH), Nutrition, and Primary Care

Vaccination Indicator: 
A Vaccine field flags visits related to vaccinations by checking diagnosis descriptions.

Rolling Time Frame:
Looks at encounters in the past year, segmented by quarter.

Automation Ready:
Built to support automated workflows (e.g. QI can pull/send lists directly to the providers).

Expanded Data Fields:
Output includes patient and visit details: Patient number, full name, DOB, encounter date/time, Billable status, visit type, specialty, provider name, location name

Data Integrity:
Only completed encounters are included, based on encounter ID and billing status.

Exclusions:
Case Management visits are excluded (no associated provider ID).

